Package: rsemflow
Type: Package
Title: Metadata-Driven Downstream Analysis for RSEM Gene-Level Results
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: person("Daiki", "Kumakura", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "55353329+DaikiKumakura@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Standard downstream results for bulk RNA-seq from RSEM
    gene-level files and an ordinary sample metadata table, from the command
    line or from R. 'rsemflow' imports '*.genes.results' files, checks them
    against the metadata, and computes expression summaries, normalized
    expression, principal component analysis, sample correlation, 'DESeq2'
    differential expression for an explicitly stated design, preranked gene
    set enrichment analysis, 'GSVA' or 'ssGSEA' pathway scores, and gene
    annotation, for human and mouse. Inconsistent input stops the run instead
    of producing results. Every result is a tab-separated table; the package
    does not draw figures.
